        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Combinatorics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read left to right as a spectrum of questions.** Enumerative combinatorics\nasks *how many*; algebraic combinatorics gives you the *machinery* (generating\nfunctions, group actions) that turns hard counts into algebra; extremal\ncombinatorics asks *how far* a structure can be pushed before a constraint\nforces a pattern; the probabilistic method proves a structure *exists* by\nshowing a random one works with positive probability. All four lean on the same\ncore trick: a **bijection** that re-expresses an unknown count as a known one."
    },
