      "text": "## The Four Core Questions"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#007",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:00-overview, git-history:combinatorics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Combinatorics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every combinatorial problem is, at bottom, one of four questions about a finite\n(or formal) set of objects."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#008",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:00-overview, git-history:combinatorics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Combinatorics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Question | Pillar | Canonical tool | This library |\n|----------|--------|----------------|--------------|\n| How many objects are there? | Enumerative | Bijections, sum/product, sieve | `01`, `02`, `04` |\n| Can I package the whole sequence of counts? | Algebraic | Generating functions | `03`, `05`, `07` |\n| How big before structure is forced? | Extremal | Turán, Dilworth, EKR | `06`, `09` |\n| Does *some* object with a property exist? | Probabilistic | First/second moment, LLL | `08` |"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:00-overview, git-history:combinatorics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Combinatorics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The boundaries are porous. Ramsey theory (`06`) is \"extremal\" but its bounds are\nproved by counting and by the probabilistic method. Catalan numbers (`05`, `07`)\nare enumerative but live algebraically as a generating function with a closed\nform. Treat the pillars as emphasis, not partition."
    },
    {
