      },
      "text": "## Layer 2 — Algebraic: Package the Counts"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#018",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:00-overview, git-history:combinatorics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Combinatorics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "When a single number is not enough — when you want the *whole sequence*\n`a_0, a_1, a_2, ...` — you encode it as the coefficients of a formal power\nseries. This is the **generating function**, the central object of algebraic\ncombinatorics."
    },
